@startuml sequence
!include style.puml
title A day's steps reaching Apple Health

participant "Health Services" as HS #F2F2F7
participant "DeltaQueue\non the watch" as DQ #EAF8EF
participant "BridgeService\non the watch" as SVC #EAF8EF
participant "BridgeCentral" as BC #EAF2FC
participant "HealthMirror" as STORE #EAF2FC
participant "Apple Health" as HK #F2F2F7

== Bringing the link up ==

SVC -> SVC : advertise, 30s burst / 5min rest
BC -[#0A6ED1]> SVC : connect with the bond keys
BC -> SVC : discover services
BC -> SVC : subscribe by writing the CCCD
SVC -> SVC : advertising off
BC -> SVC : sync, goal
note over SVC, BC
  Encrypted and MITM protected, or the watch
  refuses the read, the write and the subscribe.
end note

== What the watch collects ==

HS -[#1DA34A]> DQ : one STEPS point per step, ~400ms apart
DQ -> DQ : merge contiguous points, up to 5 minutes
HS -[#B23A34]> DQ : ~30 ambient readings a minute
DQ -> DQ : one median reading per minute, at its own time
note right of DQ
  Appended to a log on disk as they arrive.
  Health Services publishes each point once and
  keeps no history, so this is the only copy.
end note

== Delivering, a window at a time ==

loop until the queue is empty
  DQ -[#1DA34A]> BC : 64 messages
  BC --> SVC : the radio reports its queue emptied
  SVC -> DQ : forget that window
  SVC -> SVC : write it off against the day's ledger
end
note over DQ, BC
  64 at a time because the link discards its whole
  backlog past 512 chunks: one burst of a day's queue
  overflowed, returned the batch, and burst again.
  Measured: 800 messages in 12 seconds, none returned.
end note

alt the radio reports a discard
  SVC -> DQ : return the window to the front
  SVC -> SVC : retry in 2s
end

== Writing one delivery ==

BC -> STORE : delta, or a timestamped beat
STORE -> STORE : already written? then ignore it
STORE -[#1DA34A]> HK : one sample, over its own span

alt store sealed or not authorised
  HK --> STORE : errorDatabaseInaccessible
  STORE -> STORE : keep it, stop draining
  note right of STORE
    Retried on the next push, on unlock, on an
    authorisation change, and on foreground. The
    watch forgot it the moment the radio confirmed,
    so dropping it would lose it outright.
  end note
end

== The absolute, which writes nothing ==

SVC -[#8E8E93]> BC : day: the total, and what the belt delivered
BC -> STORE : the tiles, the resting rate, and the audit
note right of STORE
  ours < delivered is a write Health refused.
  delivered < the watch's total is a delivery
  that never arrived, and has no repair.
end note
@enduml
